ia.controls.airplane=Palanca adelante/atrás: potencia  Mirada: cabeceo y giro  Palanca izquierda/derecha: girar  Atacar o mantener Saltar: disparar  Apunta a un objetivo un segundo para fijarlo: las armas disparan solas  Agacharse: bajar
ia.controls.all=Works the same on touch, controller and keyboard. Planes: push the stick forward to raise the throttle and back to lower it (and brake on the ground); with look steering the plane pitches and turns toward where you look. Helicopters and airships: the stick flies forward, back and turns; look up to climb and down to descend. With stick-only steering (free look) you can look around freely: planes climb as you push forward and descend as you pull back, and helicopters and airships only climb or descend when you look far up or down. Airships keep their speed: push forward to speed up and back to slow down. The gyrodyne needs you to hold forward to spin the rotor up. Attack (on touch: tap while holding any item, or tap your aircraft) to fire weapons; on keyboard and controller you can also hold Jump to keep firing, even at the open sky. Guns, cannons, rockets and missiles also fire on their own whenever a monster is in your sights (turrets: where you look; forward guns: ahead of the aircraft), on every device; bombs and dispensers always need a click (world setting: Auto-fire); the telescope zooms in on the first press and out on the next. Use a firework rocket to burn the rockets in the boost slot. Out of fuel, a plane noses over and dives straight down, and it explodes when it hits the ground. A plane shot down in the air either blows up or goes down burning and breaking apart. Use the Aircraft Settings item to choose which weapons fire and whether you hold to fire or tap to start and stop. Aim at an enemy plane, player or mob for about a second to lock on: your guns then fire on their own whenever it is in your sights (turret guns aim ahead of it), and missiles chase it. Look away for a few seconds to drop the lock. Sneak (or the dismount button) to get out. Use an aircraft while holding an upgrade, weapon, banner or dye to install it. Sneak next to an aircraft and use it (the Open button on touch) to open its Java inventory or install fuel. Use a damaged aircraft to repair it. Sneak and hit an aircraft to open this panel, which can also kick out passengers, lock the aircraft so only you can use it, or pick it up as an item. World settings: Settings > Behavior Packs > Immersive Aircraft > gear.
